    {
      "id": "SYN-007",
      "location": "research/scope.md, section 3.1, paragraph 'What is the wedding garment?' (line 172): \"Aquinas gathers these as putting on Christ by sacrament, by charity, by remembrance of death and by works, 'et si unum deficiat, malum'.\"",
      "problem": "This is unchanged since iteration 0. The summary attaches 'et si unum deficiat, malum' to the four ways of putting on Christ. The same record's locus row for Super Matthaeum c. 22 (line 143), research/interpretations.md line 232 and the Venice page (p. 282, which I re-read at this iteration) all attach it to the closing triad of good works, holy conduct and true charity. The concise study follows the page, so no reader of it is misled.",
      "required_result": "When the research record is next revised, attach the clause in the summary only to Aquinas's closing triad, as the locus row does.",
      "severity": "advisory"
    }
  ],
  "iteration": 2,
  "observations": [
    {
      "location": "run ledger, accepted SYN-008 (synthesis-review, iteration 0), on the expansive study's sections/30-the-wedding-garment.tex 'Quae est ista vestis? Christus'",
      "note": "SYN-008's premise is false: the Venice page reads 'ista', as the expansive study and now the concise study print, and as I confirmed on the page image at this iteration. evaluations/blocking-findings-v1.toml no longer lists it, but the run still holds it as accepted, and its required_result (print 'illa' when the study is next revised) must not be acted on. A person should retire it."
    },
    {
      "location": "src/sources/works/thomas-aquinas/opera-editio-altera-veneta-tomus-3/editions/1745-venice-bettinelli/artifacts/ia-djvu-ocr-10aa155e/artifact.toml, notes",
      "note": "The notes still warn only that this OCR reads long s as f. They do not warn that it reads the st ligature as 'll' or 'li' ('Quae ell ilia veftis? Chrillus' for 'Quae est ista vestis? Christus'), and that misreading reached research/scope.md line 143, research/interpretations.md line 232, synthesis-review 0 and derive-synthesis 1. A caveat in the source record, or a check that refuses a Latin quotation from this OCR unless it was read on the page image, would catch the whole class of error."
    }
  ],
