  "summary": "Cold review, iteration 2, of the concise study (synthesis.tex, 12 physical pages). All 15 sealed input hashes match. I rebuilt the study independently in scratch from those sources: its aux file is byte-identical to the author's proof (9fa9be30...), the extracted layout text is identical, the log has no warnings, and the zref markers put the inventory and four sense rows on p. 1, the chronology on p. 2, the themes on pp. 3-4 and the commentary from p. 5. The only change from iteration 1 is 'ista'/'this' on p. 7. SYN-009 is repaired. I read the Venice p. 282 image from facsimile matthew-22-facsimile-d80cea1b myself, at native resolution on its foreground mask, and it reads 'Quae est ista vestis? Christus', with the same long-s/t ligature as 'est' and 'vestis'. On the same column 'illum' has a plain double l, and the four ways of putting on Christ and the closing triad with 'et si unum deficiat, malum' stand as the concise study gives them. The production-review withdrawals and the iteration-2 entry, and the generation-metadata contribution descriptions, are accurate, and check-generation-metadata passes on the source and on my rebuilt PDF. Limits: the unchanged pages and components outside REVIEW_SCOPE were not re-verified against their sources at this iteration, and no other edition of Super Matthaeum was consulted. SYN-007 stays advisory in research/scope.md. Verdict: PASS."
